[center][color=#00aa90]ActivityPub / federation[/color]  (where enabled)  ·  follow remote actors[/center]

[description]

[b]Webhooks[/b] are the universal glue for small forges: your service receives JSON describing the event, verifies a shared secret or signature, and reacts. Keep handlers idempotent—GitLab/GitHub/Gitea may retry deliveries.

[b]Federation (optional/experimental):[/b] some forge directions explore ActivityPub-style following across instances; support and semantics evolve quickly—treat as beta unless your release notes say otherwise.

[b]API clients:[/b] REST endpoints mirror web features for issues and repos; token scopes should be minimal (classic PAT vs OAuth app) and rotated on staff changes.

[b]Cross-posting to GitHub:[/b] teams sometimes mirror canonical development to GitHub for visibility while authoring in Gitea—document which tracker is authoritative to avoid duplicate triage.

[b]Takeaway:[/b] outbound integrations should fail safe: timeouts, retries with backoff, and alerts when queues back up so silent webhook loss does not strand releases.
